    <string name="settings_breakdown_title">Traffic by server</string>
    <string name="settings_breakdown_summary">Show how much traffic went through the proxy versus direct. While connected, this opens a diagnostics port that other apps on your device can also read — leave it off unless you need it.</string>
    <!-- I-2 / ruling R43 (revises F2 / ruling R39): TunnelService.startCore reads this setting
         once, at connect, and is deliberately not restarted just to apply a change
         (ARCHITECTURE.md §10.4) — a working tunnel is not torn down to close a diagnostics port.
         Shown whenever a session is connected, regardless of the switch's own position or
         whether it was touched this session: a one-way "pending" flag that only latched on a
         toggle produced a false statement once the switch was changed back (it kept describing
         the earlier change, not the running session), and was lost entirely on a screen
         navigation. This single, direction-independent statement is true in every case. -->
    <string name="settings_breakdown_session_notice">⚠ Applies to your next connection</string>

